WEBVTT

00:08:57.981 --> 00:09:00.591
but then she'd been left
staring at that empty blank

00:09:00.615 --> 00:09:02.305
that comes after the words

00:09:02.329 --> 00:09:05.059
"In case of emergency, please call ..."

00:09:06.808 --> 00:09:09.540
She was nearly hysterical
when she looked at me and said,

00:09:09.564 --> 00:09:12.840
"Who's going to be there for me
if I get in a car wreck?

00:09:12.864 --> 00:09:15.741
Who's going to take care of me
if I have cancer?"

00:09:17.118 --> 00:09:19.623
Now in that moment,
it took everything I had

00:09:19.647 --> 00:09:21.301
not to say, "I will."

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:25.995
But what Emma needed wasn't some therapist
who really, really cared.

00:09:26.372 --> 00:09:30.293
Emma needed a better life,
and I knew this was her chance.